{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"9bcff993374f3029b111eaf1d5d7a16c133be3c9a19a7231815ede2eaa9905f7","packTokens":5109,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4833,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall authenticate employees only through Folio3 Google Workspace accounts and reject personal Gmail accounts and other non-Folio3 identities.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid Folio3 Google Workspace identity and a personal Gmail or other non-Folio3 identity are available for sign-in tests when each identity submits a sign-in request then the Folio3 identity receives a successful response and each non-Folio3 identity receives a non-success response\",\n    \"Given An employee has a successful returning-user authentication when the employee opens the application then the screen shows the employee dashboard\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee signs in, the Folio3 parking web app shall retrieve the employee profile by corporate email from the corporate directory and populate parking assignments and registered vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster, including an initial load from existing records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The corporate directory and initially loaded parking roster contain an employee, an assigned-parking status, and vehicle details when the employee profile is retrieved after sign-in then the returned profile fields include the employee ID, employee name, assigned-parking status, assigned floor, and registered plate and vehicle details from those sources\",\n    \"Given An administrator adds or updates an employee assignment in the roster when the employee profile is retrieved then the returned profile fields reflect the roster update\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle, then the Folio3 parking web app shall require registration of at least one license plate before enabling claims, permit one or more registered plates with optional make, model, and color, and activate each newly registered plate immediately.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle when the employee attempts a claim before registering a plate then the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle registration as required\",\n    \"Given An employee submits a plate with optional make, model, and color when the employee registers the vehicle then the returned vehicle record contains the plate and submitted optional fields, and the plate is eligible for a parking claim\",\n    \"Given An employee without a registered vehicle opens the first-login flow when the registration step is shown then the screen displays a required license-plate registration step\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall treat Monday through Friday as working days, including holidays, when applying default dedicated-parking availability and utilization scenarios.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A date range includes Monday through Sunday and a weekday holiday when the system evaluates default working-day availability then the returned date values mark Monday through Friday, including the holiday, as working days and Saturday and Sunday as non-working days\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a dedicated parking holder releases today's assigned space, then the Folio3 parking web app shall accept the release in one action, reject a duplicate release for that date, and expose the space status as Reserved, Released, or Claimed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated employee has dedicated parking that is not yet released or claimed today when the employee submits a release request then the response confirms the release and the returned status value is Released\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder is viewing the home screen and today's parking is reserved when the holder performs the release action then the screen shows a single release action and displays the updated parking status\",\n    \"Given Today's assigned space has already been released when the holder submits another release request for today then the response rejects the duplicate request and the returned status value remains unchanged\",\n    \"Given A dedicated parking holder, an employee without dedicated parking, and a claimed release are available for authorization tests when each employee submits a release request then the response permits the dedicated holder's eligible release and rejects releases by the other employee or for the already-claimed space\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow dedicated parking holders to schedule one or more parking releases on dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and display saved releases on a calendar.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A dedicated holder selects dates within the next 30 calendar days when the holder submits a schedule request then the response contains a saved release record for each selected date\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder selects a date beyond the 30-day scheduling window when the holder submits the schedule request then the response rejects the out-of-window date\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder has saved future releases when the holder opens the release calendar then the screen displays the saved release dates\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow a dedicated parking holder to cancel a scheduled release only while that date's space has not been claimed and shall record each scheduling and cancellation event.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A scheduled release has not been claimed when the holder cancels it then the response confirms cancellation and the returned audit list contains both the scheduling and cancellation events\",\n    \"Given A scheduled release has already been claimed when the holder attempts to cancel it then the response rejects the cancellation and the returned release record remains claimed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall use 8:00 AM as the default daily parking release time and allow an administrator to configure that time in the office's local timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given No administrator has changed the daily release time when the release-time configuration is read then the returned value is 8:00 AM in the configured office timezone\",\n    \"Given An administrator submits a new daily release time when the configuration is saved and read back then the response confirms the saved time and the returned value matches the configured time\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall evaluate today, the 30-day scheduling window, daily release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling using the configured office-local timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The configured office timezone differs from the test client's timezone and the test clock is near a date boundary when the system evaluates today's date and the scheduling window then the response date values match the configured office-local date boundaries\",\n    \"Given A report job is scheduled near the start of Monday in the office timezone when the job scheduler evaluates its run time then the job event records a Monday-morning run according to the configured office-local time\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a scheduled release reaches the daily release time or a same-day release occurs after that time, the Folio3 parking web app shall make the space available for claiming; a same-day release before that time shall become available at the daily release time.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A future release or a same-day release before the configured daily release time is scheduled when the office-local clock reaches the daily release time then the availability response includes the released space\",\n    \"Given A dedicated holder releases today's space after the configured daily release time when the release request completes then the response indicates that the space is available immediately\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall provide available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given One space is available and two eligible employees submit claims concurrently when the claim requests are processed then exactly one response confirms a claim, the other response rejects it, and the returned available-space count is zero\",\n    \"Given An eligible employee opens the parking availability view when spaces are available then the screen displays the current available-space count\",\n    \"Given An employee with dedicated parking submits a temporary-space claim when the claim request is processed then the response rejects the claim\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall require an employee claiming temporary parking to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle's plate for the allocation, and assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break when floors have equal remaining capacity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An employee has multiple registered vehicles and an available space exists when the employee claims the space using one selected vehicle then the returned allocation record contains the selected plate as the only authorized plate and the assigned floor has the greatest remaining capacity, subject to the configured consistent tie-break\",\n    \"Given An employee has a successful temporary claim when the employee views the allocation then the screen displays the assigned parking floor\",\n    \"Given An employee submits a temporary claim without selecting a registered vehicle when the claim is processed then the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle selection as required\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When one or more parking spaces become available, the Folio3 parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given At least one parking space becomes available and eligible non-dedicated employees have email addresses when the availability notification is processed then the outbound email-service call contains the eligible recipients and a fixed-template message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall reject employee cancellation of a temporary parking claim in Phase 1.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An employee has an active temporary parking claim when the employee submits a cancellation request then the response rejects the request and the returned claim record remains active\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"For each car plate detection received from the existing entrance LPR camera, the Folio3 parking web app shall verify the temporary allocation for that day and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization, leaving the indicator off otherwise.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A detected car plate has a valid temporary allocation for the office-local date when the entrance verification interface processes the detection then the outbound indicator call requests green activation and the response reports an authorized result\",\n    \"Given A detected car plate has no valid temporary allocation for the office-local date when the entrance verification interface processes the detection then the outbound indicator call does not request green activation and the response reports an unauthorized result\",\n    \"Given The LPR camera reports a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object when the detection is processed then the response contains no parking authorization result and no green-activation call is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record permanent-sticker vehicle plate detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those detections, and limit guard-facing product access to the indicator result.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A permanent-sticker vehicle detection is received, including when its dedicated holder released the space and another employee claimed it when the detection is processed then a detection row is recorded and no temporary-authorization decision or entry-blocking call is made for that vehicle\",\n    \"Given A security guard checks an entrance result when the guard-facing surface is accessed then the screen displays only the indicator result and exposes no parking records or product screen\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator fails or a plate cannot be read during an entrance check, then the Folio3 parking web app shall issue no automatic green authorization and shall record an unsuccessful verification result for manual verification handling.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An entrance check encounters a camera, recognition, network, or indicator failure, or an unreadable plate when the verification interface processes the failure then the response reports an unsuccessful result, the verification row records the failure, and no green-activation call is issued\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record an Unused Dedicated Parking event for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and an Unused Temporary Parking event when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A dedicated holder did not release a working-day space and no registered vehicle entry exists for that date when the utilization evaluation runs then a utilization row records Unused Dedicated Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields\",\n    \"Given An employee claimed temporary parking and the selected vehicle has no entry detection on the claim date when the utilization evaluation runs then a utilization row records Unused Temporary Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields\",\n    \"Given A permanent-sticker vehicle enters the facility when its entry detection is processed for utilization then the detection row is available to the utilization evaluation\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone containing dedicated employees who neither released nor used their parking, temporary claimants who did not use their parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and an overall utilization percentage.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Utilization history exists for the reporting week when the Monday-morning report job runs then the generated report file contains the dedicated-unused and temporary-unused employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space count, temporary-claim count, and an overall utilization-percentage field\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall email each weekly utilization report to the designated stakeholders using the configured stakeholder recipient list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A weekly report is generated and designated stakeholder email addresses are configured when the report email job runs then the outbound email-service call contains the stakeholder recipients and the generated report\",\n    \"Given An administrator changes the designated stakeholder recipient list when the list is read for the next report then the returned recipient list contains the updated addresses\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A utilization evaluation identifies unused dedicated or temporary parking when the evaluation and report jobs run then no warning, suspension, or penalty row, event, email, or outbound enforcement call is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A test retention policy is configured for release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history when the retention job runs across records both within and beyond the configured retention period then the row list retains in-period records and removes or archives expired records according to the policy\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The product is one responsive web app with layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop; all pages avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and narrow layouts use touch-sized controls.\",\n  \"The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"The main flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n  \"The first-year deployment supports the assumed employee and record population.\",\n  \"The responsive web app provides English, left-to-right content only.\",\n  \"Parking flows require an online connection and the app provides light mode only.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}